          "guid": "mszgx2nx84hegdev",
          "message": {
            "text": "startCooldown re-arms itself after a trailing call so the rate limit survives the trailing edge, not just the leading one.\n\nWithout the re-arm, a trailing invocation would clear the timer and leave the throttle \"open\" — the very next call would fire immediately, allowing two invocations closer together than ms. Re-arming means: leading fires at t0, a burst collapses to one trailing fire at t0+ms, and the window stays closed until t0+2ms, so nothing beats the ms spacing. When the follow-up cooldown ends with no pending args, trailingArgs === undefined short-circuits the recursion and the throttle goes idle (timer cleared) — the next call leads again. The test \"holds the rate limit for a beat after a trailing call, then a fresh call leads again\" walks exactly this two-window sequence; \"no trailing call when only the leading happened\" pins the idle-exit path.\n",
            "markdown": "`startCooldown` re-arms itself after a trailing call so the rate limit survives the trailing edge, not just the leading one.\n\nWithout the re-arm, a trailing invocation would clear the timer and leave the throttle \"open\" — the very next call would fire immediately, allowing two invocations closer together than `ms`. Re-arming means: leading fires at t0, a burst collapses to one trailing fire at t0+ms, and the window stays closed until t0+2ms, so nothing beats the `ms` spacing. When the follow-up cooldown ends with no pending args, `trailingArgs === undefined` short-circuits the recursion and the throttle goes idle (timer cleared) — the next call leads again. The test \"holds the rate limit for a beat after a trailing call, then a fresh call leads again\" walks exactly this two-window sequence; \"no trailing call when only the leading happened\" pins the idle-exit path.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/timing.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 96,
                  "endLine": 104,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  const startCooldown = (): void => {\n    timer = setTimeout(() => {\n      timer = undefined;\n      if (trailingArgs !== undefined) {\n        runTrailing();\n        startCooldown(); // hold the rate limit for a beat after a trailing call\n      }\n    }, ms);\n  };"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
